  "transcript": {
    "answer": "The OpenTelemetry JS metrics API has no proxy meter. A counter or histogram created at module import time is bound to whatever meter provider is registered at that moment. That is normally the no-op provider, because the real MeterProvider and exporter haven't been set up yet. The instrument stays bound to the no-op meter and is never re-bound after the real provider is registered, so it records nothing. lore-api's counters were permanent no-ops for this reason. The fix was to resolve instruments lazily, looking them up against metrics.getMeterProvider() at use time instead of at import.",
